notesT: NEW — biofeedback-driven brainwave ENTRAINMENT (audio + visual), science-first.
  Open Compose → the "Entrainment" panel → Enable. The body drives it: your HRV coherence
  selects the brainwave band (aroused → Beta, relaxed → Alpha, settled → Theta), and the
  stimulus only deepens on a good pulse lock. Audio uses gentle isochronic amplitude pulses
  at the band rate; pin a band (Delta…Gamma) or leave it on Auto (bio-selected). In the
  fullscreen visual, a pinned band also makes the picture pulse WITH the entrainment — always
  held under the 3 Hz flash-safety limit.
  Off by default (silent until you enable it AND a real pulse lock is present). Reviewed for
  DSP correctness, Swift-6 concurrency, and bio-safety (flash cap, no medical overclaim, no
  wellness/esoteric wording).
  SAFETY (also shown in the panel): not while driving or operating machinery; not under the
  influence of alcohol/drugs; coordinate any therapeutic use with your provider. For self-
  observation, NOT medical diagnosis. Max 3 Hz visual flash.
  Also in this build (from 10.77.2): three new visual looks (Aurora/Lissajous/Depth Caustics),
  unified Tools menu, audio route-change hardening, AirPlay projection hint.
  Test 10.77.3: Compose → Entrainment → Enable → with a finger on the camera, watch the band
  follow your coherence (or pin Theta/Alpha); open the fullscreen visual with a pinned band and
  confirm the picture pulses gently (never a fast flash); confirm audio has a soft rhythmic
  pulse; toggle off → the pulse stops.
